Package: epiRobust
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Robustness Diagnostics for Surveillance Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("EpiStack", "Authors", email = "epistack@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: EpiStack Authors [aut, cre]
Maintainer: EpiStack Authors <epistack@example.com>
Description: Spatial robustness layer (L3.5) of the EpiStack ecosystem.
    Audits how far a spatial epidemiologic conclusion depends on analyst
    choices: the modifiable areal unit problem (MAUP), adjacency definition,
    spatial dependence in standard errors, and multiplicity in local cluster
    tests. Computes scale and zoning sensitivity, rook/queen/kNN weight
    sensitivity, Conley heteroskedasticity-and-autocorrelation-consistent
    standard errors at multiple distance cutoffs, and Bonferroni/BH-FDR
    adjustments, then compiles a single-file HTML diagnosis report. Core
    statistics use base R only; no spatial or Bayesian dependency is required.
